WEBVTT

00:02.700 --> 00:05.704
I got the whole day planned.
First, we see the primates.

00:05.829 --> 00:08.206
Then the butterfly house, bathroom break...

00:08.332 --> 00:11.875
Can't we all just run around
in a disorganised fashion?

00:11.959 --> 00:14.586
- Yeah!
- Monkeys throw their poo!

00:14.670 --> 00:17.716
If we don't adhere to a schedule,
we won't see everything.

00:17.798 --> 00:21.553
Kids, gas masks. Run!

00:27.183 --> 00:30.728
There you are.
Oh, don't be such a pig, Mr Pig.

00:30.852 --> 00:35.523
Now, where's Mr Sheep?
Is he being baa-shful?

00:36.566 --> 00:38.860
That's right. You're all ripe for parody.

00:38.985 --> 00:41.990
- Can we go now?
- Shut up! I'm having fun.

00:43.575 --> 00:48.161
Oh, my, someone's awfully rude.
Oh! My fanny is not on the menu! What?

00:48.245 --> 00:53.584
What the...? Agh! Agh!
Oh, God! Oh, God! Agh! Agh!

00:57.547 --> 01:00.675
Here, little fella. Come get the food.

01:00.759 --> 01:03.261
I have always wanted to do this.

01:03.387 --> 01:08.056
Oh, here are the marsupials.
Peter, what the hell are you doing?!

01:08.181 --> 01:11.727
Look at me, Lois, I'm Roo. Come on, Ma.

01:11.810 --> 01:16.733
Let's go watch Pooh trick the bees out of
their honey by pretending he's a rain cloud.

01:17.982 --> 01:22.572
I am going to kick your ass.

01:22.655 --> 01:26.408
"It seems today that all you see

01:26.533 --> 01:29.746
"Is violence in movies and sex on TV

01:29.871 --> 01:33.415
"But where are those
good old-fashioned values

01:33.498 --> 01:36.126
"On which we used to rely?

01:36.210 --> 01:39.547
"Lucky there's a family guy

01:39.672 --> 01:44.759
"Lucky there's a man who positively
can do all the things that make us

01:44.885 --> 01:46.552
"Laugh and cry

01:46.636 --> 01:51.767
"He's a family guy

02:06.990 --> 02:09.369
- How's it going?
- Great. Beautiful day.

02:09.493 --> 02:15.541
Gorgeous. We sit here and force small talk
while they have the time of their lives.

02:15.625 --> 02:17.500
Yeah. Yeah.

02:22.214 --> 02:25.342
Here, girl.

02:32.016 --> 02:36.894
Sorry. I... I thought I smelled... cookies.

02:37.020 --> 02:41.691
Wow. Does it really smell like cook...?
God! She farted and it went down my throat!

02:43.986 --> 02:48.283
- Full house.
- That's some poker face you've got, Peter.

02:48.366 --> 02:51.409
- Years of practice, boys.
- Peter, you're on a roll.

02:51.493 --> 02:53.911
We ought to get you down to Atlantic City.

02:53.994 --> 02:57.457
Sorry, guys. Lois is making me
visit the in-laws this weekend.

02:57.540 --> 03:01.086
Why does she bother? Me and Lois's
old man have never gotten along.

03:01.211 --> 03:04.422
Hey, I got an email from Mr Pewterschmidt.

03:04.547 --> 03:07.885
You should find some common ground
with your father-in-law.

03:07.968 --> 03:10.386
Figure out what he likes and study up on it.

03:10.470 --> 03:15.683
That's a great idea. I'll learn how to act
like a rich guy. I'm gonna start right now.

03:15.683 --> 03:19.229
- You're working through Christmas!
- But, sir, what of Tiny Tim?

03:19.353 --> 03:22.065
Bah! He and his ukulele shall go wanting.

03:25.193 --> 03:28.821
The New Yorker. I bet Lois's dad reads this.

03:28.821 --> 03:32.993
"I'd be more apathetic
if I weren't so lethargic. "

03:44.046 --> 03:49.175
Oh, I get it. That's kind of funny.
Yeah, can I have a copy of Jugs?

03:51.261 --> 03:54.888
In French, when you want
to say "yes", you say "oui, oui".

03:54.888 --> 04:00.939
You gotta be kidding me!
Oh, my God! That is hysterical!

04:01.064 --> 04:05.107
Oh, man! And what do you say
for no? "Doo-doo"?

04:05.107 --> 04:08.026
I'll be right back.
I gotta go take a wicked "yes".

04:16.912 --> 04:20.541
- Ohh.
- It's a person.

04:22.416 --> 04:25.461
- Would you fix the bathroom faucet?
- I fixed it already.

04:25.544 --> 04:30.342
- No, you didn't. It's still dripping.
- I'll give you all my Star Wars cards if it is.

04:30.342 --> 04:34.930
Wait, wait. Except Boba Fett. No matter
how sure I am, I never risk the Fett man.

04:37.224 --> 04:39.435
Oh, my God!

04:41.393 --> 04:43.813
- Was he just mastur...?
- Yes.

04:43.896 --> 04:48.401
- Oh, my.
- Do we... do we rub his nose in it?

04:52.031 --> 04:56.826
- Oh, hi, Brian.
- Listen, Lois, about yesterday...

04:56.826 --> 05:00.704
It's nothing to be embarrassed about.
It's perfectly normal.

05:00.788 --> 05:04.668
I know. It's just, I should be able
to control my baser instincts,

05:04.751 --> 05:07.878
but lately I've just been having these urges.

05:08.003 --> 05:12.051
Why don't you come to my parents' house?
The fresh air will help you relax.

05:12.176 --> 05:14.969
Mm, I know where I go when I want to relax.

05:16.220 --> 05:20.516
- I know the guy that owns this place!
- What?!

05:20.599 --> 05:25.731
I said, I know the guy that...
Oh, I'll tell you later. I love this song.

05:29.776 --> 05:33.530
Thanks, but I think a quiet weekend
by myself is just the thing I need.

05:33.530 --> 05:36.240
Well, have a good time.

05:37.199 --> 05:40.328
I'm gonna relax, mellow out,
and watch some television.

05:40.411 --> 05:45.334
We now return to
"World's Sluttiest Dogs" on Fox.

05:46.251 --> 05:49.170
Hey, wait up!

05:49.295 --> 05:52.714
Right into the bumper.

05:58.555 --> 06:01.474
- Hi, Mom.
- Oh, look at you all.

06:01.599 --> 06:05.978
I know someone who's getting a gift
certificate for liposuction in her stocking.

06:06.061 --> 06:07.938
- Thank you.
- Hello, everyone.

06:08.064 --> 06:11.485
- Hi, Daddy.
- Bonjour, Monsieur Pewterschmidt.

06:11.485 --> 06:16.614
- Did Peter have a stroke?
- He's cultured himself, like Pretty Woman.

06:16.698 --> 06:20.242
Oh, so I should treat him
like a high-class whore.

06:21.703 --> 06:24.122
That's fine. Just no kissing on the lips.

06:24.206 --> 06:28.916
- Would you like a piece of candy?
- I smell death on you.

06:31.295 --> 06:34.841
Ahoy, Mr Pewterschmidt.
Permission to come aboard?

06:34.966 --> 06:38.386
- No!
- Thanks. Quite a schooner you got here.

06:38.510 --> 06:42.473
- What is she? A 45-footer?
- Peter, I didn't know you were a sailor.

06:42.557 --> 06:45.475
I didn't know you looked
so good in shorts.

06:45.601 --> 06:48.104
- What?
- You don't have an eye spliced in this line.

06:48.187 --> 06:51.648
I'll tie a bowline in there and make one.
That should hold her.

06:55.695 --> 06:59.866
- And this is a '74 Pinot Noir.
- Mmm, lovely.

06:59.991 --> 07:04.160
Carter, did you tell your son-in-law
he's not supposed to swallow the wine?

07:04.244 --> 07:06.955
Hey, where the hell is that Peter Griffin?

07:07.081 --> 07:11.669
He said he'd give me a hundred dollars
if I took off all my clothes off.

07:14.672 --> 07:17.299
Thanks for bringing me.
This is just what I needed.

07:17.383 --> 07:20.720
I'm glad. It seems like
everybody's having a lot of fun.

07:20.845 --> 07:25.223
- How long are you and your family in...?
- Uh-uh-uh-uh. No conversation.

07:25.307 --> 07:28.435
You idiot! I'm never taking you
to my country club again!

07:28.561 --> 07:31.479
- I'm sorry, Mr Pewterschmidt.
- Your husband is a moron!

07:31.563 --> 07:37.319
He walks up to the premier of China
and says "Dong, where is my automobile?"

07:37.403 --> 07:40.948
I tried to fit in with your dad's crowd,
but it's worse than before.

07:41.073 --> 07:43.866
This sucks worse than that time
I was on Survivor.

07:43.991 --> 07:47.830
How dare you wash your clothes
in our drinking water, Bebe?

07:47.830 --> 07:52.626
Now how are we gonna survive
in this harsh, unforgiving terrain?

07:52.626 --> 07:55.253
Make sure the wheel goes all the way around.

07:55.338 --> 07:59.925
Oh, no. Head-hunters. Am I fired?

08:00.466 --> 08:03.595
Peter's been trying really hard
to get you to like him.

08:03.679 --> 08:07.141
Give him another chance?
Let him join your poker game?

08:07.224 --> 08:11.604
I'd rather be stuck in an elevator
with Nathan Lane, Gilbert Gottfried,

08:11.729 --> 08:16.524
Carrot Top, uh... Sean Hayes...
Oh, you get the picture.

08:16.607 --> 08:18.193
- Please?
- No!

08:18.276 --> 08:22.572
OK. You know, maybe later
I'll take Mom by the shoeshine place

08:22.656 --> 08:26.325
and introduce her to that mulatto boy
who looks a lot like...

08:26.409 --> 08:29.328
- Would Peter like to play poker with us?
- He'd love to.

08:29.454 --> 08:30.789
That sounds dynamite.

08:35.794 --> 08:39.256
Brian, come here and meet Sea Breeze,
my prize-winning dog.

08:39.339 --> 08:43.926
Isn't she a perfect specimen?
Look at these legs and that beautiful coat.

08:44.052 --> 08:47.890
Feel the heat coming off of her genitalia.
You could roast a marshmallow.

08:48.016 --> 08:52.268
That's how you can tell she's a champion.
Go on. Put your hand there.

08:52.394 --> 08:54.562
- Oh... That is...
- Is that something?

08:54.687 --> 08:57.190
That is something. That is... that is hot.

08:57.273 --> 08:59.485
Isn't she the most beautiful dog?

08:59.568 --> 09:05.199
Yes. Yes, she is a beautiful dog.
And that's OK.

09:06.659 --> 09:09.702
This is Peter.
He's the idiot my daughter married.

09:09.785 --> 09:11.663
- Michael Eisner.
- Bill Gates.

09:11.789 --> 09:15.416
Peter's an anti-trust lawyer
with the Justice Department.

09:15.541 --> 09:18.544
Just kidding. He's a fisherman
or some stupid thing.

09:18.670 --> 09:21.673
- Hey, fellas.
- Wow! Ted Turner!

09:21.673 --> 09:24.718
- I told you not to invite him.
- He must have followed us.

09:24.802 --> 09:27.513
Come on, ladies. Are we gonna play cards?

09:27.638 --> 09:30.849
- Peter, why don't you deal?
- We're playing Texas Hold 'Em.

09:30.973 --> 09:33.684
- Are aces high or low?
- They go both ways.

09:33.769 --> 09:35.979
He said "They go both ways. "

09:37.856 --> 09:41.693
- Like a bisexual.
- Thank you, Ted. That was the joke.

09:43.904 --> 09:48.074
- I see your bet, and I raise you CNN.
- Oh, I don't think I can...

09:48.157 --> 09:51.286
You can beat him, Mr Pewterschmidt.
He's bluffing.

09:51.411 --> 09:53.790
He bet CNN. There's no way he's bluffing.

09:53.913 --> 09:58.502
I'm sure he is. He's got a tell. If you
lose this hand, I'll divorce your daughter.

09:58.586 --> 10:02.546
I'm in. All right, Teddy. I'll see your CNN
with US Steel. What have you got?

10:02.671 --> 10:04.757
- Two pair.
- Ace-high straight.

10:04.841 --> 10:08.386
You sold me out. I could use a man
like you. How's a million a year?

10:08.511 --> 10:11.013
You disgust me! Get out of my face!

10:12.683 --> 10:15.476
That's the first time
any of us have beaten Ted.

10:15.601 --> 10:19.356
- How'd you know he was bluffing?
- When he lies, he blinks twice.

10:19.440 --> 10:23.943
I noticed it when he did an interview
and said he'd be with Jane Fonda for ever.

10:24.026 --> 10:25.194
I'm gonna turn in.

10:25.278 --> 10:29.991
Me too. I gotta be at Disneyland. We're
ethnically cleansing the Small World ride.

10:30.075 --> 10:32.160
You guys practically run this country.

10:32.286 --> 10:35.705
There's gotta be a ton
of fun stuff we could do.

10:40.502 --> 10:44.380
Oh, man, there's a toll booth.
Anybody got a quarter?

10:44.464 --> 10:49.052
- What's a quarter?
- Well, we gotta give him something.

10:54.056 --> 10:58.144
Man. Looking up at the sky
just makes you feel so small.

10:58.227 --> 11:02.523
Yeah. I mean, if God created
all this, who created God?

11:02.607 --> 11:06.151
- Maybe he created himself.
- Or herself.

11:06.151 --> 11:08.237
- Ohh...
- Think about that.

11:08.362 --> 11:11.073
Neat. This guy's deep. Where'd you find him?

11:11.157 --> 11:14.703
He's my son-in-law.

11:14.703 --> 11:17.956
- OK, honey. I gotta go. You want a ride?
- Sure.

11:25.671 --> 11:29.634
- Wow.
- I actually had a good time with you tonight.

11:29.717 --> 11:33.680
And I just want to say...
I'm glad you married my daughter.

11:33.804 --> 11:37.015
- Thank you, Jesus.
- Actually, it wasn't me, it was...

11:37.141 --> 11:39.934
No, no, it's OK. I'm used to it.

11:43.606 --> 11:48.278
- Having fun, Peter?
- I put all my poker winnings on your dog.

11:48.403 --> 11:51.113
Dog?

11:51.198 --> 11:53.908
Nothing to worry about.
Sea Breeze is a sure thing.

11:54.032 --> 11:58.411
- Sea Breeze?
- Dad, where are the jockeys?

11:58.496 --> 12:01.750
They're all in the laundry.
I'm going Indian today.

12:05.378 --> 12:08.421
- Oh, come on, Sea Breeze!
- Sea Breeze! Yeah!

12:08.505 --> 12:11.341
- Come on! Go! Go!
- Come on!

12:13.510 --> 12:16.139
What's Brian doing?

12:19.058 --> 12:22.270
- Oh, my God.
- He's violating Sea Breeze.

12:22.396 --> 12:26.440
No, he's awkwardly positioning himself...
Now he's violating Sea Breeze.

12:36.868 --> 12:41.664
Again, I want to tell you how sorry I am
about this. I don't know what came over me.

12:41.789 --> 12:44.289
You had better not have ruined my race dog.

12:44.374 --> 12:46.460
I am very disappointed in you!

12:46.585 --> 12:49.922
I'd turn my back, but I've seen
what you do in that situation.

12:50.006 --> 12:53.258
Now, Carter and I have
a polio match to attend.

12:53.342 --> 12:57.638
Get away from me! You and that filthy
mongrel of yours! How is she, Doctor?

12:57.721 --> 13:00.558
She's fine. Sea Breeze
will be able to race again.

13:00.641 --> 13:04.520
But, unfortunately, not for
another nine weeks. She's pregnant.

13:05.437 --> 13:09.108
I just want you to know I am
going to do the right thing here.

13:09.192 --> 13:12.237
You're never going to see Sea Breeze again!

13:12.320 --> 13:15.991
- Pack your things and get out!
- I am never speaking to you again.

13:16.074 --> 13:18.492
Don't worry. I have a plan.

13:18.576 --> 13:23.079
I am gonna go back in time and stop
Brian from getting it on with your dog.

13:23.162 --> 13:25.249
Everybody stand back.

13:25.375 --> 13:28.502
Aah!

13:29.627 --> 13:35.259
Oh... Oh... Oh, boy... Oh... Oh...
Oh, God. Agh. Agh.

13:36.635 --> 13:39.429
Mr Pewterschmidt,
please can we still be pals?

13:39.429 --> 13:42.891
See. I made a picture of you and me
out of glue and macaroni.

13:42.974 --> 13:45.393
That means a lot to me because you made it.

13:45.477 --> 13:46.854
- Really?
- No! Get out!

13:46.938 --> 13:49.648
- Mr Pewterschmidt, Sea Breeze is gone!
- What?

13:49.773 --> 13:51.024
I can't find Brian.

13:51.109 --> 13:56.029
Peter, do you know what I'm going to do
to you if Brian took off with my Sea Breeze?

13:56.112 --> 13:58.322
I think I have an idea.

14:06.958 --> 14:10.501
This is the room. The light switch
is here. It's mostly for show.

14:10.627 --> 14:14.798
There's your Murphy Bed. Don't mind
the Epsteins. They keep to themselves.

14:14.882 --> 14:18.969
We're going to see Bobby Darin
at the Copa tomorrow, right, Charlie?

14:19.052 --> 14:20.637
Bobby Darin, tomorrow.

14:20.721 --> 14:23.974
This is the bathroom.
Watch out, we got some bad roaches.

14:24.057 --> 14:26.769
- You're on our turf, man.
- Man, I'll cut you.

14:26.769 --> 14:31.148
I'll cut you up so bad
you gonna wish I no cut you up so bad.

14:31.148 --> 14:33.775
- Those are bad roaches.
- I blame the schools.

14:37.946 --> 14:40.532
- Were you followed?
- Don't worry. I've got a decoy.

14:41.574 --> 14:45.119
Hey, Lois. Hubba-hubba.
Whoa, Lois, you put on a few, huh?

14:45.245 --> 14:47.331
Well, I never!

14:47.415 --> 14:51.293
That's all right, I don't think he was the one.
Let's go get sundaes.

14:51.376 --> 14:55.254
We all really miss you.
And Peter talks about you all the time.

14:55.338 --> 14:57.425
- Oh, really? Anything nice?
- No.

14:57.549 --> 14:59.844
Oh, so he's still mad, huh?

14:59.927 --> 15:04.223
I should go. Take this. It's probably
not a good idea for us to meet any more.

15:04.307 --> 15:07.017
Daddy swore he'd track you down
any way he could.

15:12.564 --> 15:14.649
- Bingo!
- I told you she'd lead us to him.

15:14.732 --> 15:17.653
- Let's call Pewterschmidt.
- Let's take the jet packs.

15:17.777 --> 15:19.864
Cool!

15:20.781 --> 15:23.409
Man, the people look like ants from up here.

15:23.492 --> 15:27.035
They are ants, Michael. They are ants.

15:29.537 --> 15:33.085
This is Tricia Takanawa live
where police have discovered

15:33.210 --> 15:37.172
the whereabouts of Sea Breeze,
the heiress to the Pewterschmidt fortune.

15:37.255 --> 15:40.926
The dognapper has been traced
to this sleazy motel.

15:41.009 --> 15:45.180
Ah, I see my colleague Tom Tucker
is already on the scene.

15:45.180 --> 15:48.014
Who's that, baby?

15:48.099 --> 15:52.062
Hello, this is Tom Tucker's
evil twin Todd Tucker

15:52.187 --> 15:54.772
out to destroy his brother's reputation.

15:54.899 --> 15:56.442
Ha-ha-ha.

15:56.567 --> 16:01.362
I'm going inside to have freaky sex with my
prostitute with whom I still have 45 minutes.

16:01.445 --> 16:03.030
Back to this breaking news.

16:13.958 --> 16:16.044
Brian, please eat something.

16:16.169 --> 16:22.007
My face is on the news. Your father won't
let me see the dog carrying my puppies.

16:22.090 --> 16:24.802
And he's going to incredible lengths
to ignore me.

16:24.928 --> 16:28.682
Brian, don't let him get to you.
Peter, come out of that thing!

16:28.765 --> 16:33.479
He can't hear you. Besides, it's not him
that's getting to me, it's your father.

16:33.561 --> 16:37.731
I'm sorry. I talked to him, but he
wouldn't budge. He can be so stubborn.

16:37.857 --> 16:42.528
I don't know how my mother puts up with it.
He did promise to take care of the puppies.

16:42.654 --> 16:46.907
They're not his to take care of. They're
my kids, and I'm gonna get 'em back.

16:47.032 --> 16:50.036
My father wasn't there for me,
but I'll be there for my kids!

16:50.161 --> 16:53.581
I'm gonna sue your dad for custody!

17:00.255 --> 17:04.342
Please stop this. Brian has every right
to see his puppies when they're born.

17:04.426 --> 17:05.676
Sorry, pumpkin.

17:05.801 --> 17:09.347
I had no idea you could be so cruel.
I'll never forgive you for this!

17:09.430 --> 17:13.308
- You're just having your period.
- This court will now come to order.

17:13.392 --> 17:17.689
- Brian, do you like children?
- I love children. That's why I'm here.

17:17.773 --> 17:20.191
I want the opportunity to raise my puppies.

17:20.275 --> 17:25.196
Do you remember an incident at a South
Attleboro Denny's in December of 1996?

17:25.279 --> 17:26.656
Yeah, I guess.

17:34.663 --> 17:40.085
Waa! Waa! You like that, huh?!
You like that?! Waa!

17:40.085 --> 17:45.925
You just tune this out, don't you?!
Waa! Well, tune this out! Waa!

17:47.509 --> 17:49.262
- Aah...
- Waa!

17:49.386 --> 17:51.472
- Aah...
- Waa!

17:51.555 --> 17:52.597
- Aah...
- Shut up!

17:52.722 --> 17:56.143
I was angry because my Moon Over
My Hammy was overcooked and...

17:56.269 --> 17:59.397
I also have your rental records
from the Quahog Video Store.

17:59.480 --> 18:03.569
- Can you read the last two titles?
- Son In Law and Bio-Dome.

18:03.652 --> 18:06.485
- And who's the star of those films?
- Pauly Shore.

18:06.570 --> 18:08.656
Pauly Shore!

18:08.781 --> 18:10.741
He's terrible.

18:10.865 --> 18:15.246
I rented those for Peter. He got banned
from the store for taping over movies.

18:18.374 --> 18:20.543
Rosebud.

18:21.711 --> 18:25.130
It's his sled. It was his sled
from when he was a kid.

18:25.255 --> 18:28.259
There, I just saved you
two long boobless hours.

18:28.384 --> 18:31.095
How convenient. Blame it on someone else.

18:31.177 --> 18:33.806
Is that the man we want
raising these puppies?

18:33.890 --> 18:37.351
Peter? Oh, you've gotta
believe me, Your Honour.

18:37.434 --> 18:40.562
Peter, I'm putting together
another card game. You in?

18:40.688 --> 18:43.272
- You... you want me to play?
- Absolutely.

18:43.397 --> 18:47.153
But first I want you to testify
against that horny mutt of yours.

18:47.236 --> 18:49.239
Oh, I don't know if I can do that.

18:49.322 --> 18:52.867
That's too bad, because Bill and Michael
want to see you again.

18:52.992 --> 18:56.119
Bill's going to bring his Stretch Armstrong.

18:56.202 --> 18:58.914
Oh, man, and his arms
stretch out to next week!

18:59.038 --> 19:03.209
Your Honour, Peter Griffin
would like to take the stand.

19:04.335 --> 19:08.716
Mr Griffin, which of the following two
phrases best describes Brian Griffin?

19:08.841 --> 19:11.552
Problem drinker,
or African-American haberdasher?

19:11.634 --> 19:14.973
- I guess problem drinker, but that's...
- Thank you.

19:15.098 --> 19:19.893
Sexual deviant, or magic picture that if you
stare at it long enough, you see something?

19:19.976 --> 19:23.022
- Sexual deviant, but that one's not...
- Thank you.

19:23.105 --> 19:27.902
Now, isn't it true that you told my client
that Brian is a menace to society

19:27.902 --> 19:31.030
and should never be allowed
to see his children?

19:31.155 --> 19:34.075
Um... Uh...

19:39.579 --> 19:42.082
Brian should be allowed to see his puppies!

19:42.916 --> 19:47.629
- Peter, think about what you're doing.
- I am. Your Honour, Brian'll be a great dad.

19:47.713 --> 19:51.174
If I was half the parent he is,
I'd know Chris's favourite ice cream is...

19:51.258 --> 19:53.885
- Chocolate-chip.
- Stewie's favourite bedtime story is...

19:53.969 --> 19:55.970
- Goodnight, Moon.
- Meg's real father's name is...

19:56.053 --> 19:58.140
Stan Thompson.

19:59.183 --> 20:03.479
I've heard enough. I do believe
that Brian would be a successful parent.

20:03.562 --> 20:08.566
If he was to repeat his actions, he would
be setting a bad example for his puppies.

20:08.691 --> 20:12.863
Therefore, I grant Brian custody
with the condition that he be neutered first.

20:12.947 --> 20:16.282
Yeah! You did it, buddy! Oh, congratulations!

20:16.407 --> 20:18.703
Oh, man! What does "neutered" mean?

20:20.870 --> 20:25.585
You're almost there, Sea Breeze.
Oh, and also, I didn't bring this up before,

20:25.668 --> 20:27.878
but promise me you won't eat any of them.

20:27.961 --> 20:33.509
This is like a Greek tragedy where a man
chooses between himself and his children.

20:33.592 --> 20:37.970
Of course, you'll be playing
the role of "Sans Testiclese".

20:38.096 --> 20:40.890
We're ready for you down the hall.

20:41.016 --> 20:45.187
Sure you want to go through with this?
You could have puppies with another dog.

20:45.270 --> 20:49.023
And maybe with a condor!
Yeah, then you'd have flying puppies.

20:49.148 --> 20:52.152
Would you like that, Brian?
Huh? Flying puppies?

20:52.277 --> 20:54.571
No. Those puppies in there are mine.

20:54.655 --> 20:57.700
And I'll give anything
to be with them. Anything.

20:57.783 --> 21:01.869
I am not looking forward to what you're
gonna be like once they do this to you.

21:01.953 --> 21:06.665
Mmm. I love chocolate.

21:07.709 --> 21:11.128
But I can't eat it because then I'll get fat.

21:11.254 --> 21:14.382
But it's so good!

21:14.465 --> 21:17.177
- Are you ready, Brian?
- I guess so.

21:18.137 --> 21:20.305
Stop! Brian, come quick!

21:22.806 --> 21:26.894
- Oh, my God! Those aren't my puppies!
- Then whose are they?

21:30.315 --> 21:35.237
You! You're a whore! A filthy, filthy whore!

21:35.319 --> 21:37.198
You must be so relieved.

21:37.198 --> 21:40.949
Actually, I... I was kind of
looking forward to being a dad.

21:41.075 --> 21:43.578
Don't worry. There'll be other chances.

21:43.661 --> 21:48.875
Hey, you know what's funny?
I always thought that dogs... laid eggs.

21:49.000 --> 21:51.085
And I learned something today.

21:51.086 --> 22:52.086
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru